              "notes": "Close-in defence, and it fights its own battle: no interest at all in what the ship as a whole has picked, no view on how big a target is, and every view on how near. Guns and engines before hull, because a fighter it disarms is a fighter that has stopped mattering, and a fighter it strands is one the batteries can take at their leisure."
